==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.33~6.67 seconds<sup>10f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.33~2 seconds<sup>10f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 8~13.33 seconds<sup>240f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Similar strategies can be used from [[Prickly Field]] as the stage is nearly identical. Because of the flood of Those Guys at the start of the round, it's not recommended to use [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] to stall, but you can use melee cats to push back the wave and earn money faster and it's safe to do so as Bore won't spawn when above 200,000 base health.

When you feel like it's time to go all in, do so spamming every [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cat]] that you have. Using [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] and [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] is recommended as they can stunlock Bore when enough of them are spawned.

